---
/**
 * One tab shows at a time. Commands are the install scripts and examples that CI runs.
 * PyPI and npm commands stay off this component until those packages exist.
 */
import { existsSync, readFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { dirname, resolve } from "node:path";
import { fileURLToPath } from "node:url";

function findExample(name: string): string {
  const starts = [process.cwd(), dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url))];
  for (const start of starts) {
    let dir = start;
    for (let i = 0; i < 8; i += 1) {
      const candidate = resolve(dir, "examples", "quickstart", name);
      if (existsSync(candidate)) return readFileSync(candidate, "utf8");
      const parent = dirname(dir);
      if (parent === dir) break;
      dir = parent;
    }
  }
  throw new Error(`missing examples/quickstart/${name}`);
}

const pin = "b830e15efa2f7bd05af0769739c6cab6feb40d97";
const shHash = "4630175aa8868d58b634df1043abdd0fae425d78c93326401d41e5ed5a752590";
const psHash = "75fdf00099a9a464fff1e0d54495037cff2d1dc6046a035ad9df2b5ea5f1822f";
const shUrl = `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/goshikavs/goshikq-agent-framework/${pin}/scripts/install.sh`;
const psUrl = `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/goshikavs/goshikq-agent-framework/${pin}/scripts/install.ps1`;
const linuxInstall = `curl -fsSL -o goshikq-install.sh ${shUrl}
echo "${shHash}  goshikq-install.sh" | sha256sum -c -
sh goshikq-install.sh --version v1.0.0`;
const macosInstall = `curl -fsSL -o goshikq-install.sh ${shUrl}
echo "${shHash}  goshikq-install.sh" | shasum -a 256 -c -
sh goshikq-install.sh --version v1.0.0`;
const windowsInstall = `Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "${psUrl}" -OutFile goshikq-install.ps1
$actual = (Get-FileHash .\\goshikq-install.ps1 -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLower()
if ($actual -ne "${psHash}") { throw "SHA256 mismatch: $actual" }
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\goshikq-install.ps1 -Version v1.0.0`;
const pyExample = findExample("sdk_hello.py");
const tsExample = findExample("hello.mjs");
---
<div class="journey">
  <fieldset class="install-tabs">
    <legend>Install target</legend>
    <label><input type="radio" name="gk-install" id="tab-linux" checked /> Linux</label>
    <label><input type="radio" name="gk-install" id="tab-macos" /> macOS</label>
    <label><input type="radio" name="gk-install" id="tab-windows" /> Windows</label>
    <label><input type="radio" name="gk-install" id="tab-python" /> Python</label>
    <label><input type="radio" name="gk-install" id="tab-typescript" /> TypeScript / JavaScript</label>
  </fieldset>

  <div class="panel panel-linux">
    <h2>Linux runtime</h2>
    <p>Recommended install: download the pinned installer, check its SHA256, then run the local file. That is not a remote shell pipe. The script installs both <code>goshikq</code> and <code>goshikq-server</code> from GitHub Release v1.0.0 and stops if <code>SHA256SUMS</code> does not match. It does not install a language SDK. The manual alternative is to download the archive and <code>SHA256SUMS</code> from the release and compare the hash yourself.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>Install the runtime.</p>
        <div class="copy-block">
          <pre class="install"><code>{linuxInstall}</code></pre>
          <button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Use the <code>export PATH</code> line the script prints, then verify. Expected text: <code>goshikq 1.0.0</code>.</p>
        <div class="copy-block">
          <pre class="install"><code>goshikq --version</code></pre>
          <button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Start the local runtime. <code>DATABASE_URL=embedded</code> downloads PostgreSQL on first start and keeps it under <code>.goshikq/postgres</code> unless <code>GOSHIKQ_EMBEDDED_PG_DIR</code> is set. That first download needs network access. <code>GOSHIKQ_AUTH_MODE=none</code> is only for this local process. Production needs a real database URL and real authentication.</p>
        <div class="copy-block">
          <pre class="install"><code>DATABASE_URL=embedded GOSHIKQ_AUTH_MODE=none GOSHIKQ_BIND=127.0.0.1:7400 goshikq-server</code></pre>
          <button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button>
        </div>
        <div class="copy-block">
          <pre class="install"><code>curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:7400/health</code></pre>
          <button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p>Expected health body includes <code>"status":"ok"</code> and <code>"version":"1.0.0"</code>. Then run the <code>python3</code> line the installer prints. That file is <code>hello_agent.py</code> next to the binaries. Expected lines include <code>verification:  VERIFIED</code> and <code>evidence:      greetings-memory@1</code>.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="panel panel-macos">
    <h2>macOS runtime</h2>
    <p>The same pinned installer selects the Apple Silicon or Intel v1.0.0 archive and checks SHA256SUMS. It installs both executables and does not install a language SDK. You can instead download the archive and <code>SHA256SUMS</code> from the release and compare the hash yourself.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>Install the runtime.</p>
        <div class="copy-block">
          <pre class="install"><code>{macosInstall}</code></pre>
          <button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Use the printed PATH line. Expected text: <code>goshikq 1.0.0</code>.</p>
        <div class="copy-block">
          <pre class="install"><code>goshikq --version</code></pre>
          <button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Start the runtime. The first <code>DATABASE_URL=embedded</code> start downloads PostgreSQL into <code>.goshikq/postgres</code>. Production must not use <code>GOSHIKQ_AUTH_MODE=none</code>.</p>
        <div class="copy-block">
          <pre class="install"><code>DATABASE_URL=embedded GOSHIKQ_AUTH_MODE=none GOSHIKQ_BIND=127.0.0.1:7400 goshikq-server</code></pre>
          <button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button>
        </div>
        <div class="copy-block">
          <pre class="install"><code>curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:7400/health</code></pre>
          <button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p>Expected health body includes <code>"status":"ok"</code> and <code>"version":"1.0.0"</code>. Then run the <code>python3</code> line the installer prints. Expected lines include <code>verification:  VERIFIED</code> and <code>evidence:      greetings-memory@1</code>.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="panel panel-windows">
    <h2>Windows runtime</h2>
    <p>Windows AMD64 is the supported archive. The pinned script checks SHA256SUMS, installs both executables, and prints a PATH line. It does not install a language SDK. You can instead download the zip and <code>SHA256SUMS</code> from the release and compare the hash yourself.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>Install the runtime.</p>
        <div class="copy-block">
          <pre class="install"><code>{windowsInstall}</code></pre>
          <button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Use the PATH line the script prints. Expected text: <code>goshikq 1.0.0</code>.</p>
        <div class="copy-block">
          <pre class="install"><code>goshikq --version</code></pre>
          <button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Start the runtime. The first embedded database start downloads PostgreSQL. Production must not use <code>GOSHIKQ_AUTH_MODE=none</code>.</p>
        <div class="copy-block">
          <pre class="install"><code>$env:DATABASE_URL="embedded"
$env:GOSHIKQ_AUTH_MODE="none"
$env:GOSHIKQ_BIND="127.0.0.1:7400"
goshikq-server</code></pre>
          <button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button>
        </div>
        <div class="copy-block">
          <pre class="install"><code>curl.exe -fsS http://127.0.0.1:7400/health</code></pre>
          <button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p>Expected health body includes <code>"status":"ok"</code> and <code>"version":"1.0.0"</code>. Then run the <code>python</code> line the installer prints. Expected lines include <code>verification:  VERIFIED</code> and <code>evidence:      greetings-memory@1</code>.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="panel panel-python">
    <h2>Python SDK</h2>
    <p>Install the Python SDK only after the runtime is healthy. <code>goshikq-ai</code> 1.0.1 is not on PyPI, so there is no registry install command here. CPython 3.11 through 3.14. Save the program below as <code>sdk_hello.py</code> in any directory and run <code>python sdk_hello.py</code> after the package is installed. No paid model key is required. Expected lines include <code>verification:  VERIFIED</code>.</p>
    <div class="copy-block">
      <pre class="install"><code>{pyExample}</code></pre>
      <button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel panel-typescript">
    <h2>TypeScript / JavaScript SDK</h2>
    <p>Install the TypeScript SDK only after the runtime is healthy. <code>@goshikq/sdk</code> 1.0.1 is not on npm, so there is no registry install command here. The package is ESM only. Node.js 20+ runs it with <code>node hello.mjs</code>. CommonJS <code>require()</code> is not supported. Save the program below as <code>hello.mjs</code> in a project that has the package installed. Expected lines include <code>verification:  VERIFIED</code>.</p>
    <div class="copy-block">
      <pre class="install"><code>{tsExample}</code></pre>
      <button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  document.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
    const target = event.target;
    if (!(target instanceof Element)) return;
    const btn = target.closest("[data-copy]");
    if (!(btn instanceof HTMLButtonElement)) return;
    const code = btn.parentElement?.querySelector("code");
    const text = code?.textContent ?? "";
    void navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(() => {
      btn.textContent = "Copied";
    });
  });
</script>
